Here is a beautifully structured vocabulary learning interface containing ten high-frequency vocabulary flashcards, interactive progress tracking, and learning cues. 

The layout is split into two columns: the left column acts as the study control panel (showing your daily goal progress, current level XP, and helpful recall tips), while the right column hosts the interactive card deck itself.

### 1. Initialize the UI Surface

First, we create a dedicated UI surface for this vocabulary-building session:

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9.1",
  "createSurface": {
    "surfaceId": "vocabulary-booster-session",
    "catalogId": "https://a2uicatalog.ai/catalog/c-learning.json"
  }
}
</a2ui-json>

### 2. Render the Vocabulary Interface Components

Next, we populate the interface with the interactive elements. We use the `columns` component as the root element to create a side-by-side split screen, perfect for maintaining a clear overview of progress while actively flipping through the card deck.

<a2ui-json>
{
  "version": "v0.9.1",
  "updateComponents": {
    "surfaceId": "vocabulary-booster-session",
    "components": [
      {
        "id": "root",
        "component": "columns",
        "cols": 2,
        "gap": "2rem",
        "align": "top",
        "items": [
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "header-section",
                "component": "page_header",
                "title": "## Word Power Booster",
                "subtitle": "Master these 10 essential vocabulary terms for advanced reading and writing comprehension.",
                "icon": "🎓",
                "tag": "Daily Vocab Set 1",
                "accent": "#4f46e5"
              },
              {
                "id": "active-recall-tip",
                "component": "text_callout",
                "variant": "info",
                "title": "Study Strategy",
                "description": "Don't just read! Attempt to explain or define the term to yourself out loud before clicking to flip the card."
              },
              {
                "id": "vocab-progress-indicator",
                "component": "progress_bar",
                "value": 60,
                "label": "Session Review Progress",
                "accent": "#10b981",
                "show_percent": "true",
                "caption": "6 of 10 words reviewed today"
              },
              {
                "id": "gamification-xp",
                "component": "xp_bar",
                "level_label": "Vocabulary Apprentice (Level 3)",
                "xp_current": 650,
                "xp_next": 1000,
                "accent": "#4f46e5",
                "show_flash": true
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "vocabulary-deck",
                "component": "flashcard_deck",
                "accent": "#4f46e5",
                "label_front": "VOCABULARY WORD",
                "label_back": "DEFINITION & EXAMPLES",
                "cards": [
                  {
                    "front": "Ephemeral",
                    "back": "Lasting for a very short time; transient.\n\n*Example:* 'The ephemeral joys of childhood pass all too quickly.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Capricious",
                    "back": "Given to sudden and unaccountable changes of mood or behavior.\n\n*Example:* 'The administration's capricious policies left businesses bewildered.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Alacrity",
                    "back": "Brisk and cheerful readiness.\n\n*Example:* 'She accepted the invitation to join the research team with alacrity.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Taciturn",
                    "back": "Reserved or uncommunicative in speech; saying little.\n\n*Example:* 'A taciturn man by nature, he preferred to let his actions speak for him.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Pernicious",
                    "back": "Having a harmful effect, especially in a gradual or subtle way.\n\n*Example:* 'The pernicious influence of sensationalized news can erode public trust.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Mitigate",
                    "back": "Make less severe, serious, or painful.\n\n*Example:* 'Good planning can help mitigate the risks of international travel.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Loquacious",
                    "back": "Tending to talk a great deal; talkative.\n\n*Example:* 'Normally loquacious, he fell completely silent when asked about his past.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Equivocal",
                    "back": "Open to more than one interpretation; ambiguous.\n\n*Example:* 'The candidate's equivocal answers frustrated the journalists seeking clarity.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Assiduous",
                    "back": "Showing great care and perseverance.\n\n*Example:* 'Through assiduous research, they finally uncovered the long-lost manuscript.'"
                  },
                  {
                    "front": "Anachronism",
                    "back": "A thing belonging or appropriate to a period other than that in which it exists.\n\n*Example:* 'The depiction of a smartphone in a medieval drama is a glaring anachronism.'"
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
</a2ui-json>
